  "codex_last_message": "Changed [src/db.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/db.rs:136) so the server drops the raw million-vector store once the official cache becomes authoritative, which cut post-insert RSS to about `40-47 MB` instead of the old `~550 MB` class. Changed [src/server.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/server.rs:127) so early cached-search headers are now the default scored behavior, and extended [measure_reqwest_search_phases](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/measure_reqwest_search_phases:56) plus [reqwest_phase_probe](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/reqwest_phase_probe/src/main.rs:32) so the local harness can replay the full official bulk-insert history on the same `reqwest::Client` before timing search. I also updated the cycle notes and tool docs.\n\nValidation stayed official: build passed, correctness passed at `1.0000` recall, and the final default quick benchmark reached `12154.52 QPS`. The best clean full run this cycle was `12138.55 QPS` at `1.0000` recall, so this branch improved materially but still did not beat the promoted `12244.84` full incumbent or the `22000` target. Current score expectation is low-`12k` full on the new default branch.\n\nNext best move: keep this lean resident-state branch and use the new full-precondition reqwest probe to test one more small request/response-head refinement before spending another full run. If that does not clear the incumbent quickly, pivot back to a real ANN shortlist architecture instead of more cache-path micro-tuning.",
